{# The status, in the two spellings the app needs, and never in a third.

   The class names are spelled out here rather than composed in the view model,
   because Tailwind scans this directory for candidates
   (src/dev-ops/client/dev-ops.css) — a class name only a .ts file ever spells
   is tree-shaken out of the stylesheet and the badge renders unstyled with no
   build error and no failing test. The view model names the role; this file
   owns the class, and daisyUI owns what the class means.

   In a column — the list, the journey — it is daisyUI's
   `status` dot and a word, at the same x on every row. Pills gave six states
   six silhouettes down one column, so the eye read the shape of a row before
   it read the row, and the shapes shouted loudest on the five states that are
   perfectly healthy. The dot carries the colour and the label carries the
   meaning; neither is ever alone.

   On a page about one event there is no column to line up and one status to
   state, so `variant: "badge"` says it as a soft `badge` — the official quiet
   emphasis, and the shape a single piece of state wants.

   The label is the status as a human says it — `Dead letter`, not
   `DEAD_LETTER` — in the same words the filter segments above the table use,
   so the two are one vocabulary. The raw value the endpoint wrote is on the
   `title`, for anyone matching it against a log line or a `?status=`.

   Weight says which of them is worth stopping on. Dead letter is the page's
   subject and reads at full contrast; Completed is most of the stream and
   recedes furthest; everything else sits between. No status is bold except the
   one that is an incident.

   The retry marker is a glyph rather than an icon: the label sets one short
   line, and a trailing ↻ sits on it without the vertical alignment fight an
   inline svg picks at this size. #}
{% set dots = {
  neutral: "status",
  info: "status status-info",
  warning: "status status-warning",
  success: "status status-success",
  error: "status status-error"
} %}
{% set labels = {
  success: "text-base-content/55",
  error: "font-medium"
} %}
{% set badges = {
  neutral: "badge badge-ghost",
  info: "badge badge-info badge-soft",
  warning: "badge badge-warning badge-soft",
  success: "badge badge-success badge-soft",
  error: "badge badge-error badge-soft"
} %}
{%- set text = params.label | default(params.status, true) -%}
{%- if params.variant == "badge" -%}
<span class="{{ badges[params.role] | default("badge badge-ghost", true) }}" title="{{ params.status }}" data-testid="do-status-badge"><span data-testid="do-status-label">{{ text }}{% if params.retrying %} ↻{% endif %}</span></span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap" title="{{ params.status }}" data-testid="do-status-badge"><span class="{{ dots[params.role] | default("status", true) }}" aria-hidden="true" data-testid="do-status-dot"></span><span class="{{ labels[params.role] | default("text-base-content/80", true) }}" data-testid="do-status-label">{{ text }}{% if params.retrying %} ↻{% endif %}</span></span>
{%- endif -%}
